# tally 2.2.1 P43 S1 (L §4.4 l.669, §6.1 l.1797): the day of movements stated same, one comparison of the days each side
# can take: a side whose day is a hole gives that hole to every read of the day (review g2fix same/s5_hole_day).
# Before W10: c0 1, dy the other side's day.
=== s5_hole_day.tally
model s5
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1: money PLN
input d1: date
input d2: date
move in1: transfers
  on d1
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1
move in2: transfers
  on d2
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  a1 = 100.00 PLN "s"
  d1 = 2026-03-05 "s"
  d2 = ?"when did in2 land"
  same in1 = in2
ask dy: m.day for m in transfers over 2026-03
ask s0: sum(m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-03)
ask c0: count(m in transfers over 2026-03)
ask f1: flows(in1, 2026-03)
ask b31: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
=== expect
b31: ?"in1 and in2 are one, but leg cash differs on 2026-03-05: 100.00 PLN (in1) and 100.00 PLN (in2)" (in1, in2) ?"when did in2 land" (d2)
  cut 2026-01-01
c0: ?"when did in2 land" (d2)
  cut 2026-01-01
dy (m = in1): ?"when did in2 land" (d2)
f1: ?"when did in2 land" (d2)
  cut 2026-01-01
s0: ?"when did in2 land" (d2)
  cut 2026-01-01
